RCP Audit Artifact — Licence Composition
=========================================

This repository is a composition of materials under different licences.
The MIT Licence text below applies to the RCP audit authors' original
software contributions only. Third-party code, data, model weights, and
configuration files retain their upstream licences and carry their own
attribution requirements.

Scope of the MIT Licence
-------------------------
Applies to:
  * scripts/*.py            (analysis scripts authored by the RCP audit authors)
  * src/*.py                (Python package authored by the RCP audit authors)
  * Makefile, requirements*.txt, artifact_ledger.json, claim_manifest.json
  * tests/*.py              (test code)
  * paper/*.tex             (paper sources — text and macros)
  * figures/*.py            (figure-generation scripts)

Does NOT apply to (see respective subdirectory licences/attribution):
  * data/sacrebird/*.csv    (Czehmann et al. 2026, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; see
                             /data/sacrebird/LICENSE and /data/sacrebird/NOTICE)
  * checkpoints/**/*.ckpt   (trained weights; see below)
  * data/SLRTP2025/         (SLRTP2025 pose bundle; provider-specific terms)
  * results/transfer_cells.csv (derived data; covered by MIT as our analysis
                             output, but the underlying evaluator weights
                             used to produce it remain under SLRTP2025 terms)

Trained checkpoint weights
---------------------------
The trained checkpoint weights under /checkpoints/ are outputs of training
runs that used PHOENIX-2014T and SLRTP2025 data. They are released for
research-reproduction purposes only, consistent with the upstream dataset
licences. They carry no additional MIT Licence grant beyond what the upstream
dataset terms permit.

Released BT evaluator
---------------------
The directory /checkpoints/released/backTranslation_PHIX_model/ is a verbatim
copy of the SLRTP2025 released BT evaluator (model weights, vocab files,
config.yaml). It is NOT covered by the MIT Licence; it remains under the
SLRTP2025 challenge terms (obtain from
https://github.com/walsharry/SLRTP-Sign-Production-Evaluation).

PHOENIX-2014T
-------------
Not redistributed in this repository. The data is available from RWTH Aachen
under its academic research licence. The pose materialisation used in this
audit was obtained via the SLRTP2025 challenge bundle.

CSL-Daily
---------
Not redistributed in this repository.

CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 share-alike boundary
-------------------------------------
If you build upon or redistribute the CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 data files
(/data/sacrebird/*.csv) within a larger work, the ShareAlike clause may
require the resulting work to also carry CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. This is independent
of the MIT Licence covering the software layer.

